    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `'<LAST3>-<NNNN>'` to `'<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>'`.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`):\n- CITY3 = upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- LAST3 = upper-cased first three letters of the last name (extracted into a shared `prefix3` helper)\n- NNNN = a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the owners already in that city (previously a global count). The count now filters `findAll()` by matching city (case-insensitive).\n- Updated the class Javadoc to describe the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007`).\n\n**Derived values** \u2014 the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is built as `customerCode + \"-M\" + <year%%100>`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format with no change needed there.\n\nThe new `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` test (asserting the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
